---
import EditorialLayout from "../layouts/EditorialLayout.astro";
import "../styles/pages/t-shirt-manufacturer.css";
---

<EditorialLayout
  title={"Custom T-Shirt Manufacturer for Private Label Brands | YAUUM"}
  description={"Custom T-shirt manufacturing for private label brands, wholesalers, retailers, and e-commerce sellers. Review styles, fabrics, sampling, branding, quality checks, and packing."}
  canonical="https://yauum.com/t-shirt-manufacturer/"
  jsonLd={[{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://yauum.com/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "T-Shirt Manufacturer", "item": "https://yauum.com/t-shirt-manufacturer/"}]}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "Service", "name": "Custom and Private Label T-Shirt Manufacturing", "serviceType": "T-shirt manufacturing and product development", "provider": {"@type": "Organization", "name": "Yauum", "url": "https://yauum.com/"}, "areaServed": "Worldwide", "url": "https://yauum.com/t-shirt-manufacturer/", "description": "Custom T-shirt manufacturing for private label brands, wholesalers, retailers, and e-commerce sellers. Review styles, fabrics, sampling, branding, quality checks, and packing."}]}
  navCurrent={["/production/", "/t-shirt-manufacturer/"]}
  showMobileInquiry
>
<!-- ============ 1 HERO ============ -->
<section class="pd-hero" data-od-id="tshirt-hero">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="pd-hero-grid">
      <div class="pd-hero-copy">
        <p class="label">B2B / OEM–ODM / PRIVATE LABEL</p>
        <h1>Custom T-Shirt Manufacturer for Private Label Brands</h1>
        <p class="lead pd-hero-lead">Develop a T-shirt from silhouette, fabric weight, measurements, artwork, labels, sample approval, and bulk references.</p>
        <div class="pd-hero-actions">
          <a class="button" href="/contact-us/">Start your T-shirt project</a>
          <a class="link" href="#tshirt-styles">Explore styles</a>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-rail" aria-label="Project principles">
          <span class="rail-item"><span class="rail-num">01</span><span class="rail-label">Sample-first development</span></span>
          <span class="rail-item"><span class="rail-num">02</span><span class="rail-label">Project-confirmed details</span></span>
          <span class="rail-item"><span class="rail-num">03</span><span class="rail-label">Private label finishing</span></span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure class="pd-hero-media">
        <div class="pd-ph pd-ph--hero" role="img" aria-label="Pending image slot for a full T-shirt product photo">
          <span class="pd-ph-tag">PENDING</span>
          <strong>T-shirt product reference</strong>
          <small>Needed: a verified full-garment T-shirt photo</small>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 2 SECTION INDEX ============ -->
<nav class="pd-index" aria-label="T-shirt page sections" data-od-id="page-section-index">
  <div class="shell">
    <a href="#tshirt-styles">Styles</a>
    <a href="#tshirt-fabrics">Fabric and fit</a>
    <a href="#tshirt-branding">Branding</a>
    <a href="#tshirt-process">Process</a>
    <a href="#tshirt-quality">Quality</a>
    <a href="#tshirt-faq">FAQ</a>
  </div>
</nav>

<!-- ============ 3 PRODUCT STYLES ============ -->
<section class="section" id="tshirt-styles" data-od-id="tshirt-styles">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="pd-head">
      <div class="pd-title" data-reveal>
        <p class="label">01 / PRODUCT STYLES</p>
        <h2>Custom T-Shirt Styles We Manufacture</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="pd-note" data-reveal>
        <p class="lead">The style groups are development directions for inquiry and sampling, not a fixed stock catalog. The final pattern, measurements, fabric, and finishing are confirmed for each project.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="pd-grid-4">
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media pd-ph" role="img" aria-label="Pending image slot: Oversized heavyweight tee, full front view">
          <span class="pd-ph-tag">PENDING</span>
          <strong>Oversized heavyweight tee, full front view</strong>
        </span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">01</span><h3>Oversized and heavyweight</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">Body width, shoulder position, sleeve volume, fabric body, and finish are reviewed together.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media pd-ph" role="img" aria-label="Pending image slot: Regular-fit tee, full front view">
          <span class="pd-ph-tag">PENDING</span>
          <strong>Regular-fit tee, full front view</strong>
        </span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">02</span><h3>Classic and regular fit</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">A dependable base for everyday retail, wholesale, and private label programs.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media pd-ph" role="img" aria-label="Pending image slot: Boxy drop-shoulder tee, full front view">
          <span class="pd-ph-tag">PENDING</span>
          <strong>Boxy drop-shoulder tee, full front view</strong>
        </span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">03</span><h3>Boxy and drop shoulder</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">Shoulder proportion, armhole depth, body length, and sleeve balance shape the silhouette.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-card" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-media pd-ph" role="img" aria-label="Pending image slot: Long-sleeve tee, full front view">
          <span class="pd-ph-tag">PENDING</span>
          <strong>Long-sleeve tee, full front view</strong>
        </span>
        <span class="pd-meta"><span class="pd-num">04</span><h3>Long-sleeve and specialty</h3></span>
        <p class="pd-fill">Wash, graphic, printed, embroidered, and puff-print directions are reviewed per brief.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <div class="pd-callout" data-reveal>
      <p class="label">BUYER CHECK</p>
      <p>Show the silhouette, size range, color direction, and decoration that should be reviewed first.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 4 MATERIAL AND FIT ============ -->
<section class="section band-dark" id="tshirt-fabrics" data-od-id="tshirt-fabrics">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="pd-head">
      <div class="pd-title" data-reveal>
        <p class="label label--onDark">02 / MATERIAL AND FIT</p>
        <h2>T-Shirt Fabrics, GSM, Fits, and Construction Options</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="pd-note" data-reveal>
        <p class="lead">Fabric, fit, and construction are reviewed together. Development directions may include cotton and blended jerseys, polyester knits, mesh, interlock, rib, linen blends, washed fabrics, and heavyweight knits.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="pd-ledger">
      <article class="pd-ledger-row" data-reveal>
        <span class="num">01</span>
        <div><h3>Cotton and blended fabrics</h3><p>Review fiber composition, knit structure, hand feel, stretch, care, and intended use.</p></div>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-ledger-row" data-reveal>
        <span class="num">02</span>
        <div><h3>GSM and fabric weight</h3><p>Confirm lightweight, midweight, or heavyweight direction with the selected fabric.</p></div>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-ledger-row" data-reveal>
        <span class="num">03</span>
        <div><h3>Fit and size grading</h3><p>Lock chest, shoulder, body, sleeve, and armhole measurements across the size run.</p></div>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-ledger-row" data-reveal>
        <span class="num">04</span>
        <div><h3>Neckline and construction</h3><p>Review collar shape, rib recovery, seams, reinforcement, and finishing details.</p></div>
      </article>
    </div>
    <div class="pd-media-row">
      <div class="pd-ph" role="img" aria-label="Pending image slot for T-shirt fabric and GSM reference">
        <span class="pd-ph-tag">PENDING</span>
        <strong>Fabric and GSM reference</strong>
        <small>Needed: jersey face and reverse views, plus a verified GSM swatch comparison</small>
      </div>
      <div class="pd-ph" role="img" aria-label="Pending image slot for T-shirt construction details">
        <span class="pd-ph-tag">PENDING</span>
        <strong>Construction details</strong>
        <small>Needed: neckline rib, shoulder seam, and sleeve hem close-ups</small>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="pd-source" data-reveal>GSM is confirmed with the selected fabric. Fiber composition, knit structure, color, hand feel, shrinkage, and decoration compatibility remain project-specific.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 5 DECORATION AND PRIVATE LABEL ============ -->
<section class="section band-alt" id="tshirt-branding" data-od-id="tshirt-branding">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="pd-head">
      <div class="pd-title" data-reveal>
        <p class="label">03 / DECORATION AND PRIVATE LABEL</p>
        <h2>Printing, Embroidery, and Private Label Options</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="pd-note" data-reveal>
        <p class="lead">Decoration and brand finishing are specified with the order. The suitable method depends on artwork, fabric, placement, quantity, and required appearance.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="pd-ledger">
      <article class="pd-ledger-row" data-reveal>
        <span class="num">01</span>
        <div><h3>Decoration method selection</h3><p>Artwork format, technique, colors, size, placement, fabric, and quantity guide the review.</p></div>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-ledger-row" data-reveal>
        <span class="num">02</span>
        <div><h3>Embroidery and specialty detail</h3><p>Scale, density, appearance, and attachment are checked when the method suits the product.</p></div>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-ledger-row" data-reveal>
        <span class="num">03</span>
        <div><h3>Neck, care, and size labels</h3><p>Confirm content, dimensions, material, placement, and attachment for each label.</p></div>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-ledger-row" data-reveal>
        <span class="num">04</span>
        <div><h3>Hangtags, stickers, and codes</h3><p>Add buyer-supplied hangtags, stickers, barcodes, packaging bags, and carton marks.</p></div>
      </article>
    </div>
    <div class="pd-callout" data-reveal>
      <p class="label">ARTWORK INPUTS</p>
      <p>Send file format, intended technique, colors, artwork size, and placement with the inquiry. Final suitability is confirmed before sampling.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pd-media-row pd-media-row--split">
      <figure class="pd-figure" data-reveal>
        <img src="/uploads/t-shirt-manufacturer/branding-screen-printing-line.webp" width="1600" height="1067" alt="Carousel screen-printing line set up for garment printing in the production workshop" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption class="pd-cap">Screen-printing line, production workshop</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="pd-ph" role="img" aria-label="Pending image slot for embroidery, label, and hangtag examples">
        <span class="pd-ph-tag">PENDING</span>
        <strong>Labels and hangtags</strong>
        <small>Needed: neck label, care label, size label, hangtag, sticker, and barcode examples</small>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 6 MOQ, SAMPLING, AND BULK ============ -->
<section class="section band-dark" id="tshirt-process" data-od-id="tshirt-process">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="pd-head">
      <div class="pd-title" data-reveal>
        <p class="label label--onDark">04 / MOQ, SAMPLING, AND BULK</p>
        <h2>T-Shirt MOQ, Sampling, and Bulk Production Process</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="pd-note" data-reveal>
        <p class="lead">Sampling time, sample cost, revision terms, MOQ, and the bulk timeline are confirmed according to the product specifications and order requirements.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <ol class="pd-flow">
      <li class="pd-flow-step" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-flow-num">01</span>
        <h3>Confirm the brief</h3>
        <p>Share product direction, quantity, size split, references, fabric, artwork, packing, destination, and timing.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="pd-flow-step" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-flow-num">02</span>
        <h3>Review materials and details</h3>
        <p>Align fabric, color, hand feel, measurements, stitching, decoration, labels, and packing.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="pd-flow-step" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-flow-num">03</span>
        <h3>Develop the sample</h3>
        <p>Review fit, key measurements, fabric behavior, workmanship, branding, and overall appearance.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="pd-flow-step" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-flow-num">04</span>
        <h3>Approve the reference</h3>
        <p>Record revisions and approve the sample and specification before bulk production.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="pd-flow-step" data-reveal>
        <span class="pd-flow-num">05</span>
        <h3>Produce, check, and pack</h3>
        <p>Follow the approved reference through production, inspection, packing, and shipment preparation.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <div class="pd-media-row pd-media-row--4">
      <figure class="pd-figure" data-reveal>
        <img src="/uploads/t-shirt-manufacturer/process-pattern-sampling.webp" width="1600" height="1067" alt="Paper patterns and sample garments laid out on the pattern and sampling worktable" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption class="pd-cap">Pattern and sampling</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="pd-figure" data-reveal>
        <img src="/uploads/t-shirt-manufacturer/process-bulk-cutting.webp" width="1600" height="1067" alt="Layered fabric being cut into garment panels on the cutting table" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption class="pd-cap">Bulk cutting</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="pd-figure" data-reveal>
        <img src="/uploads/t-shirt-manufacturer/process-sewing-line.webp" width="1600" height="1067" alt="Sewing operators working along the garment production line" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption class="pd-cap">Sewing line</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="pd-figure" data-reveal>
        <img src="/uploads/t-shirt-manufacturer/process-packing.webp" width="1600" height="1067" alt="Folded garments bagged and bundled on the packing worktable" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption class="pd-cap">Packing</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <p class="pd-source" data-reveal>MOQ and production lead time should be confirmed after the product, materials, decoration, quantity, revisions, packing, and destination are understood.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 7 QUALITY AND HANDOFF ============ -->
<section class="section" id="tshirt-quality" data-od-id="tshirt-quality">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="pd-head">
      <div class="pd-title" data-reveal>
        <p class="label">05 / QUALITY AND HANDOFF</p>
        <h2>Quality Control, Packing, and Shipping Preparation</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="pd-note" data-reveal>
        <p class="lead">Quality and packing points are connected to the approved sample and order specification. Acceptance rules and tolerances are agreed per order.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="pd-ledger">
      <article class="pd-ledger-row" data-reveal>
        <span class="num">01</span>
        <div><h3>Fabric, color, and measurements</h3><p>Check shrinkage, color variation, surface condition, neckline, rib recovery, and size consistency.</p></div>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-ledger-row" data-reveal>
        <span class="num">02</span>
        <div><h3>Stitching and decoration</h3><p>Review seams, workmanship, print or embroidery placement, sharpness, and appearance.</p></div>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-ledger-row" data-reveal>
        <span class="num">03</span>
        <div><h3>Labels and quantities</h3><p>Verify label type, size, attachment, unit count, barcode, and order information.</p></div>
      </article>
      <article class="pd-ledger-row" data-reveal>
        <span class="num">04</span>
        <div><h3>Packing and shipment</h3><p>Confirm folding, individual packaging, carton marks, inspection photos, and document support.</p></div>
      </article>
    </div>
    <div class="pd-media-row pd-media-row--3">
      <figure class="pd-figure" data-reveal>
        <img src="/uploads/t-shirt-manufacturer/quality-finishing-ironing.webp" width="1600" height="1067" alt="Garments being steam-ironed and finished at the finishing station" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption class="pd-cap">Finishing and ironing</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="pd-figure" data-reveal>
        <img src="/uploads/t-shirt-manufacturer/quality-storage-cartons.webp" width="1600" height="1067" alt="Packing cartons and fabric rolls stored on warehouse shelving" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption class="pd-cap">Cartons and storage</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="pd-ph" role="img" aria-label="Pending image slot for measurement and label inspection evidence">
        <span class="pd-ph-tag">PENDING</span>
        <strong>Measurement and label checks</strong>
        <small>Needed: size measurement, color and print check, and label verification photos</small>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 8 WORKING WITH YAUUM ============ -->
<section class="section band-dark" id="why-yauum" data-od-id="why-yauum">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="pd-proof">
      <div class="pd-proof-intro" data-reveal>
        <p class="label label--onDark">06 / WORKING WITH YAUUM</p>
        <h2>Why Work With YAUUM as Your T-Shirt Manufacturer</h2>
        <p class="lead">The workflow connects product definition, material review, sampling, revision, approval, bulk production, quality checks, packing, and shipment preparation.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pd-proof-list">
        <article class="pd-proof-row" data-reveal>
          <span class="num">01</span>
          <div><h3>A structured product development process</h3><p>Each stage creates a reference for the next stage.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article class="pd-proof-row" data-reveal>
          <span class="num">02</span>
          <div><h3>One approved reference for sampling and bulk</h3><p>Bulk production follows the approved sample and specification.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article class="pd-proof-row" data-reveal>
          <span class="num">03</span>
          <div><h3>Production and packing records buyers can review</h3><p>Photos and records can be requested by project stage.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article class="pd-proof-row" data-reveal>
          <span class="num">04</span>
          <div><h3>Verified company and factory information</h3><p>Publish company facts only after supporting information is confirmed.</p></div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="pd-proof-media" data-reveal>
      <figure class="pd-figure">
        <img src="/uploads/t-shirt-manufacturer/showroom-tshirt-samples.webp" width="1600" height="1067" alt="Finished T-shirts in multiple colors displayed on rails in the sample showroom" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption class="pd-cap">Sample T-shirts on display in the showroom</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 9 BUYER QUESTIONS ============ -->
<section class="section band-alt" id="tshirt-faq" data-od-id="tshirt-faq">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="pd-head">
      <div class="pd-title" data-reveal>
        <p class="label">07 / BUYER QUESTIONS</p>
        <h2>Common Questions Before Ordering Custom T-Shirts</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="pd-note" data-reveal>
        <p class="lead">Start with the questions that shape fabric, sampling, branding, quantity, quality, and delivery decisions.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="pd-faq">
      <details open>
        <summary><h3>What T-shirt styles can I customize?</h3></summary>
        <p>Style directions can include basic, fit-driven, wash, graphic, printed, and embroidered directions. The final pattern and measurements are confirmed during project review and sampling.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary><h3>Which fabric and GSM should I choose?</h3></summary>
        <p>The choice depends on fit, season, hand feel, drape, surface, decoration, shrinkage expectations, and intended use. GSM is confirmed with the selected fabric during sampling.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary><h3>Can I add printing or embroidery?</h3></summary>
        <p>Decoration methods are project-dependent. Send the file format, intended technique, colors, artwork size, and placement so the suitable option can be reviewed.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary><h3>Can you add custom labels or hangtags?</h3></summary>
        <p>Private label details can include woven main labels, neck labels, size labels, care labels, hangtags, stickers, barcodes, packaging bags, and carton marks when specified in the order.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary><h3>What is the MOQ?</h3></summary>
        <p>MOQ depends on the product specification, decoration method, color and size breakdown, and order requirements. Confirm the quantity before sampling or production.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary><h3>Can I order a sample first?</h3></summary>
        <p>Yes. The workflow is sample-first. Sample time, cost, and revision terms are set per project after materials and details are confirmed.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary><h3>What information is needed for a quotation?</h3></summary>
        <p>Send the product category, quantity and size split, references, fabric composition and target GSM, color and hand feel, artwork, label and packaging files, destination, and timing.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary><h3>How are finished T-shirts checked and packed?</h3></summary>
        <p>Checks follow the approved sample and can cover measurements, fabric, color, construction, decoration, labels, quantities, and packing specifications.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 10 START A PROJECT ============ -->
<section class="section band-dark" id="start-project" data-od-id="start-project">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="pd-cta-grid">
      <div class="pd-cta-copy" data-reveal>
        <p class="label label--onDark">08 / START A PROJECT</p>
        <h2>Start Your Custom T-Shirt Project</h2>
        <p>Send your tech pack, reference photos, or sample garment with quantity, size range, fabric direction, decoration, packing, destination, and timing.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pd-cta-actions" data-reveal>
        <a class="button" href="/contact-us/">Send your T-shirt brief</a>
        <a class="link link--onDark" href="#tshirt-styles">Review styles</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</EditorialLayout>
